{
  "mn56:0.1": "Middle Discourses 56 ",
  "mn56:0.2": "With Upāli ",
  "mn56:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn56:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Nāḷandā in Pāvārika’s Mango Grove. ",
  "mn56:2.1": "At that time the Jain ascetic of the Ñātika clan was residing at Nāḷandā together with a large assembly of Jain ascetics. ",
  "mn56:2.2": "Then the Jain ascetic Dīgha Tapassī wandered for alms in Nāḷandā. After the meal, on his return from almsround, he went to Pāvārika’s Mango Grove. There he approached the Buddha, and exchanged greetings with him. ",
  "mn56:2.3": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he stood to one side. The Buddha said to him, ",
  "mn56:2.4": "“There are seats, Tapassī. Please sit if you wish.” ",
  "mn56:3.1": "When he said this, Dīgha Tapassī took a low seat and sat to one side. ",
  "mn56:3.2": "The Buddha said to him, ",
  "mn56:3.3": "“Tapassī, how many kinds of deed does the Jain ascetic of the Ñātika clan describe for performing bad deeds?” ",
  "mn56:3.4": "“Reverend Gotama, the Jain Ñātika doesn’t usually speak in terms of ‘deeds’. ",
  "mn56:3.5": "He usually speaks in terms of ‘rods’.” ",
  "mn56:3.6": "“Then how many kinds of rod does the Jain Ñātika describe for performing bad deeds?” ",
  "mn56:3.7": "“The Jain Ñātika describes three kinds of rod for performing bad deeds: ",
  "mn56:3.8": "the physical rod, the verbal rod, and the mental rod.” ",
  "mn56:3.9": "“But are these kind